---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { planets } from "../../data/planets";
---
<SiteLayout title="Interactive Solar System tools" description="Explore ORRERYA's free planetary calculators, orbital mechanics lab, JPL-based planet position explorer and planetary correlation tools.">
  <div class="container breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Interactive tools</span></div>
  <header class="page-intro container"><div class="eyebrow">SOLAR SYSTEM TOOLS</div><h1>Solar System calculators<br />and interactive models.</h1><p class="lede">Change a value, choose another world or convert a distance. Each tool shows the calculation behind its result.</p></header>
  <section class="section container">
    <div class="tools-grid">
      <article class="card tool-panel" id="weight">
        <span class="eyebrow">Tool 01 · Gravity</span><h2>How much would you weigh on other worlds?</h2><p>Mass is the amount of matter in you. Weight is the gravitational force acting on that mass. Your mass stays the same as you travel; your weight changes with local gravity.</p>
        <div class="field"><label for="mass-input">Your mass (kilograms)</label><input id="mass-input" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" step="any" value="70" inputmode="decimal" /></div>
        <div class="field"><label for="gravity-world">Choose a world</label><select id="gravity-world">{planets.map((planet)=><option value={planet.gravityValue} data-name={planet.name} selected={planet.slug === "earth"}>{planet.name}</option>)}</select></div>
        <div class="result-box" aria-live="polite"><span>Gravitational force on you</span><strong id="weight-result">686 N</strong><span id="weight-subresult">Equivalent to about 70 kg on an Earth-calibrated scale.</span></div>
        <p class="tool-footnote">Model: W = m × g. Uses the listed equatorial gravity values; real local gravity can vary with latitude, altitude and a world's rotation. This is not a prediction of how a spacesuit or spacecraft behaves.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card tool-panel" id="distance">
        <span class="eyebrow">Tool 02 · Distance & light</span><h2>How far is an AU?</h2><p>An astronomical unit (AU) is defined as exactly 149,597,870.7 kilometres. It is a useful unit for measuring distances within planetary systems.</p>
        <div class="field"><label for="au-input">Distance (AU)</label><input id="au-input" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" step="any" value="1" inputmode="decimal" /></div>
        <div class="result-box" aria-live="polite"><span>Distance in kilometres</span><strong id="km-result">149,597,871 km</strong><span id="light-result">Light travel time: 8 min 19 s</span></div>
        <p class="tool-footnote">Uses the exact AU definition and the speed of light in vacuum, 299,792.458 km/s. Light time is a simple straight-line vacuum calculation.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card tool-panel" id="compare">
        <span class="eyebrow">Tool 03 · Planetary scale</span><h2>Compare planet sizes.</h2><p>Compare a planet's equatorial diameter with Earth's. The circles use a common scale, capped so the largest planet fits on the card.</p>
        <div class="field"><label for="size-world">Choose a planet</label><select id="size-world">{planets.map((planet)=><option value={planet.diameterKm} data-name={planet.name} data-mass={planet.mass1024} selected={planet.slug === "earth"}>{planet.name}</option>)}</select></div>
        <div class="size-stage"><div id="size-orb" class="size-orb" style="width:56px;height:56px"></div><div><strong id="size-name">Earth</strong><span id="size-diameter">12,756 km diameter</span><b id="size-ratio">1.00 × Earth's diameter</b><small id="mass-ratio">1.00 × Earth's mass</small></div></div>
        <div class="scale-legend"><span>Relative diameter</span><span>Earth = 1</span></div>
        <div class="scale-track"><span id="scale-fill" style="width:8.9%"></span></div>
        <p class="tool-footnote">The circle represents diameter only. The labels compare diameter and mass with Earth; the circle does not encode mass, density or surface area. Planet images are not drawn to this scale.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card tool-panel" id="year">
        <span class="eyebrow">Tool 04 · Orbital period</span><h2>How long is a year?</h2><p>A planet's orbital period is the time it takes to complete one orbit around the Sun relative to distant stars.</p>
        <div class="field"><label for="year-world">Choose a planet</label><select id="year-world">{planets.map((planet)=><option value={planet.orbitDays} data-name={planet.name} selected={planet.slug === "earth"}>{planet.name}</option>)}</select></div>
        <div class="result-box" aria-live="polite"><span>One sidereal orbit</span><strong id="year-result">365.2 days</strong><span id="year-subresult">About 1.00 Earth years.</span></div>
        <p class="tool-footnote">Uses NASA/JPL sidereal orbital periods, converted from Julian years using 365.25 days per Julian year. The Earth-year comparison uses Earth's JPL sidereal orbital period. A sidereal orbital period is measured relative to distant stars; it is not a planet's solar day or a seasonal year.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="lab-launch-grid" aria-label="Advanced planetary labs">
      <a class="lab-launch-card" href="/tools/ephemeris/">
        <span class="eyebrow">Tool 06 · JPL approximate ephemeris</span><h2>Planet position explorer</h2>
        <p>Choose a date and see the eight planets projected around the Sun, with geometric distances and EMB-relative directions. The Earth row is a barycentre proxy, not a lunar-resolved geocentre.</p><span class="text-link">Explore planetary positions ↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="lab-launch-card" href="/tools/correlation-lab/">
        <span class="eyebrow">Tool 07 · Planetary data</span><h2>Planetary correlation lab</h2>
        <p>Choose any two of seven physical or orbital properties, switch between linear and logarithmic axes, and inspect the relationship.</p><span class="text-link">Explore planetary data ↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <section class="card orbit-lab" id="orbit">
      <div class="orbit-lab-heading">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Tool 05 · Orbital mechanics</span><h2>Move a planet around its orbit.</h2><p>Choose a planet and move it through its orbit. Watch its distance from the Sun and orbital speed change between perihelion and aphelion.</p></div>
        <span class="tag">Two-body teaching model</span>
      </div>
      <div class="orbit-lab-layout">
        <div class="orbit-canvas">
          <svg id="orbit-svg" viewBox="0 0 440 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="orbit-title orbit-desc">
            <title id="orbit-title">Schematic planetary orbit</title>
            <desc id="orbit-desc">A planet moves along an elliptical orbit around the Sun. The orbit shape changes with eccentricity. This illustration is not to scale across planets.</desc>
            <ellipse id="orbit-track" cx="122.38" cy="150" rx="140" ry="139.98" fill="none" stroke="rgba(151,184,220,.58)" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <line id="orbit-radius" x1="120" y1="150" x2="0" y2="150" stroke="rgba(230,200,142,.55)" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="4 4" />
            <circle id="orbit-sun" cx="120" cy="150" r="10" fill="#edb966" />
            <circle cx="120" cy="150" r="17" fill="none" stroke="rgba(237,185,102,.2)" />
            <circle id="orbit-marker" cx="0" cy="150" r="6.5" fill="#8bc9dc" stroke="#e5f3f8" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <text x="120" y="181" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e6c88e" font-size="10">SUN</text>
            <text id="orbit-phase-label" x="220" y="24" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9ba9bd" font-size="10" letter-spacing="1">TRUE ANOMALY · 0°</text>
          </svg>
          <div class="orbit-legend"><span><i class="legend-sun"></i> Sun · focus</span><span><i class="legend-planet"></i> Planet</span><span>Orbit shape · schematic</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="orbit-controls">
          <div class="field"><label for="orbit-world">Choose a planet</label><select id="orbit-world">{planets.map((planet)=><option value={planet.distanceAu} data-a={planet.semiMajorAxisAu} data-e={planet.eccentricityValue} data-name={planet.name} selected={planet.slug === "earth"}>{planet.name}</option>)}</select></div>
          <div class="field"><label for="orbit-angle">Move around the orbit <output id="orbit-angle-value" for="orbit-angle">0°</output></label><input id="orbit-angle" type="range" min="0" max="360" step="0.1" value="0" /></div>
          <div class="orbit-play-row">
            <button type="button" class="btn small secondary" id="orbit-play" aria-pressed="false">Play orbit</button>
            <p id="orbit-play-status" class="orbit-play-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Play to see the planet move faster near perihelion and slower near aphelion.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="orbit-result-grid">
            <div class="orbit-result"><span>Distance from Sun</span><strong id="orbit-distance">0.983 AU</strong><small id="orbit-distance-km">147.1 million km</small></div>
            <div class="orbit-result"><span>Orbital speed</span><strong id="orbit-speed">30.3 km/s</strong><small id="orbit-speed-note">Faster near perihelion</small></div>
          </div>
          <div class="orbit-endpoints"><div><span>Perihelion · closest</span><strong id="orbit-peri">0.983 AU</strong></div><div><span>Aphelion · farthest</span><strong id="orbit-aphe">1.017 AU</strong></div></div>
          <p class="orbit-model-note">Uses an idealised two-body orbit with the Sun's standard gravitational parameter. The slider is the angle from perihelion. Playback completes one selected orbit in 24 seconds, preserving the changing speed along that ellipse; it does not compare the planets' actual year lengths. Positions and sizes are schematic.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="orbit-equations"><div><span class="eyebrow">Distance along an ellipse</span><strong>r = a(1 − e²) / (1 + e cos ν)</strong></div><div><span class="eyebrow">Vis-viva equation</span><strong>v² = μ(2/r − 1/a)</strong></div></div>
    </section>
    <div class="callout tools-note"><strong>These are transparent educational models.</strong><p>They use rounded reference values and standard equations. They are not a navigation system, a live ephemeris or a precision engineering tool. Open the linked NASA/JPL references for definitions, uncertainties and higher-precision parameters.</p></div>
    <div class="source-panel"><div><span class="eyebrow">Calculation references</span><h3>Sources and constants</h3><p>Planetary gravity and orbital values are taken from NASA/JPL and NASA NSSDCA tables.</p></div><ul class="source-list"><li><a href="https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/planets/phys_par.html" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">NASA/JPL — Planetary Physical Parameters ↗</a></li><li><a href="https://nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/planetary/factsheet/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">NASA NSSDCA — Planetary Fact Sheet ↗</a></li><li><a href="https://www.iau.org/public/themes/measuring/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">International Astronomical Union — Measuring the Universe ↗</a></li></ul></div>
  </section>
  <script>
    import {
      meanAnomalyFromTrueAnomaly,
      orbitalState,
      trueAnomalyFromMeanAnomaly
    } from "../../lib/orbital-mechanics.js";
    import {
      ASTRONOMICAL_UNIT_KM,
      SPEED_OF_LIGHT_KM_S,
      EARTH_SIDEREAL_YEAR_DAYS
    } from "../../lib/scientific-constants.js";
    const formatter = new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US", { maximumFractionDigits: 2 });
    const massInput = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("#mass-input");
    const gravitySelect = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("#gravity-world");
    const weightResult = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#weight-result");
    const weightSub = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#weight-subresult");
    function updateWeight() {
      if (!massInput || !gravitySelect || !weightResult || !weightSub) return;
      const mass = Number(massInput.value);
      const gravity = Number(gravitySelect.value);
      if (!Number.isFinite(mass) || mass < 0 || !Number.isFinite(gravity)) {
        weightResult.textContent = "Enter a valid mass";
        weightSub.textContent = "Use a non-negative number in kilograms.";
        return;
      }
      const force = mass * gravity;
      weightResult.textContent = formatter.format(force) + " N";
      weightSub.textContent = "About " + formatter.format(force / 9.80665) + " kg-force on an Earth-calibrated scale · " + (gravitySelect.selectedOptions[0]?.dataset.name || "selected world");
    }
    massInput?.addEventListener("input", updateWeight);
    gravitySelect?.addEventListener("change", updateWeight);
    updateWeight();

    const auInput = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("#au-input");
    const kmResult = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#km-result");
    const lightResult = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#light-result");
    function updateDistance() {
      if (!auInput || !kmResult || !lightResult) return;
      const au = Number(auInput.value);
      if (!Number.isFinite(au) || au < 0) {
        kmResult.textContent = "Enter a valid distance";
        lightResult.textContent = "Use a non-negative number of AU.";
        return;
      }
      const km = au * ASTRONOMICAL_UNIT_KM;
      const seconds = km / SPEED_OF_LIGHT_KM_S;
      const hours = Math.floor(seconds / 3600);
      const minutes = Math.floor((seconds % 3600) / 60);
      const remain = Math.round(seconds % 60);
      kmResult.textContent = formatter.format(km) + " km";
      lightResult.textContent = hours > 0 ? "Light travel time: " + hours + " h " + minutes + " min " + remain + " s" : "Light travel time: " + minutes + " min " + remain + " s";
    }
    auInput?.addEventListener("input", updateDistance);
    updateDistance();

    const sizeSelect = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("#size-world");
    const sizeOrb = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#size-orb");
    const sizeName = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#size-name");
    const sizeDiameter = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#size-diameter");
    const sizeRatio = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#size-ratio");
    const massRatio = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#mass-ratio");
    const scaleFill = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#scale-fill");
    function updateSize() {
      if (!sizeSelect || !sizeOrb || !sizeName || !sizeDiameter || !sizeRatio || !massRatio || !scaleFill) return;
      const diameter = Number(sizeSelect.value);
      const mass = Number(sizeSelect.selectedOptions[0]?.dataset.mass);
      const ratio = diameter / 12756;
      const massMultiple = mass / 5.97217;
      const visualSize = Math.max(13, Math.min(188, 56 * ratio));
      sizeOrb.style.width = visualSize + "px";
      sizeOrb.style.height = visualSize + "px";
      sizeName.textContent = sizeSelect.selectedOptions[0]?.dataset.name || "Selected world";
      sizeDiameter.textContent = formatter.format(diameter) + " km diameter";
      sizeRatio.textContent = formatter.format(ratio) + " × Earth's diameter";
      massRatio.textContent = formatter.format(massMultiple) + " × Earth's mass";
      scaleFill.style.width = Math.min(100, (diameter / 142984) * 100) + "%";
    }
    sizeSelect?.addEventListener("change", updateSize);
    updateSize();

    const yearSelect = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("#year-world");
    const yearResult = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#year-result");
    const yearSub = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#year-subresult");
    function updateYear() {
      if (!yearSelect || !yearResult || !yearSub) return;
      const days = Number(yearSelect.value);
      yearResult.textContent = formatter.format(days) + " days";
      yearSub.textContent = "About " + formatter.format(days / EARTH_SIDEREAL_YEAR_DAYS) + " Earth years · " + (yearSelect.selectedOptions[0]?.dataset.name || "selected world");
    }
    yearSelect?.addEventListener("change", updateYear);
    updateYear();

    const orbitSelect = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("#orbit-world");
    const orbitAngle = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("#orbit-angle");
    const orbitAngleValue = document.querySelector<HTMLOutputElement>("#orbit-angle-value");
    const orbitTrack = document.querySelector<SVGEllipseElement>("#orbit-track");
    const orbitMarker = document.querySelector<SVGCircleElement>("#orbit-marker");
    const orbitRadius = document.querySelector<SVGLineElement>("#orbit-radius");
    const orbitPhaseLabel = document.querySelector<SVGTextElement>("#orbit-phase-label");
    const orbitDistance = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#orbit-distance");
    const orbitDistanceKm = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#orbit-distance-km");
    const orbitSpeed = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#orbit-speed");
    const orbitSpeedNote = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#orbit-speed-note");
    const orbitPeri = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#orbit-peri");
    const orbitAphe = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#orbit-aphe");
    const orbitPlay = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("#orbit-play");
    const orbitPlayStatus = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#orbit-play-status");
    const ORBIT_CYCLE_MS = 24000;
    const orbitFormatter = new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US", { maximumFractionDigits: 3 });
    let orbitAnimationFrame = 0;
    let orbitAnimationStart: number | null = null;
    let startingMeanAnomaly = 0;

    function stopOrbitAnimation(announce = true) {
      const wasPlaying = orbitAnimationFrame !== 0;
      if (orbitAnimationFrame) cancelAnimationFrame(orbitAnimationFrame);
      orbitAnimationFrame = 0;
      orbitAnimationStart = null;
      if (orbitPlay) {
        orbitPlay.textContent = "Play orbit";
        orbitPlay.setAttribute("aria-pressed", "false");
      }
      if (announce && wasPlaying && orbitPlayStatus) {
        orbitPlayStatus.textContent = "Paused. Use the slider or play the orbit again.";
      }
    }

    function updateOrbit() {
      if (!orbitSelect || !orbitAngle || !orbitAngleValue || !orbitTrack || !orbitMarker || !orbitRadius || !orbitPhaseLabel || !orbitDistance || !orbitDistanceKm || !orbitSpeed || !orbitSpeedNote || !orbitPeri || !orbitAphe) return;
      const option = orbitSelect.selectedOptions[0];
      const aAu = Number(option?.dataset.a);
      const eccentricity = Number(option?.dataset.e);
      const degrees = Number(orbitAngle.value);
      if (!Number.isFinite(aAu) || aAu <= 0 || !Number.isFinite(eccentricity) || eccentricity < 0 || eccentricity >= 1 || !Number.isFinite(degrees)) return;
      const state = orbitalState(aAu, eccentricity, degrees);
      const nu = degrees * Math.PI / 180;
      const rAu = state.distanceAu;
      const radiusRatio = rAu / aAu;
      const rKm = state.distanceKm;
      const periAu = state.perihelionAu;
      const apheAu = state.aphelionAu;
      const scale = 140;
      const focusX = 120;
      const focusY = 150;
      const centerX = focusX + scale * eccentricity;
      const semiMinor = scale * Math.sqrt(1 - eccentricity * eccentricity);
      const markerX = focusX - scale * radiusRatio * Math.cos(nu);
      const markerY = focusY - scale * radiusRatio * Math.sin(nu);
      orbitTrack.setAttribute("cx", String(centerX));
      orbitTrack.setAttribute("cy", String(focusY));
      orbitTrack.setAttribute("rx", String(scale));
      orbitTrack.setAttribute("ry", String(semiMinor));
      orbitMarker.setAttribute("cx", String(markerX));
      orbitMarker.setAttribute("cy", String(markerY));
      orbitRadius.setAttribute("x1", String(focusX));
      orbitRadius.setAttribute("y1", String(focusY));
      orbitRadius.setAttribute("x2", String(markerX));
      orbitRadius.setAttribute("y2", String(markerY));
      orbitAngleValue.textContent = degrees.toFixed(1) + "°";
      orbitPhaseLabel.textContent = "TRUE ANOMALY · " + degrees.toFixed(1) + "°";
      orbitDistance.textContent = orbitFormatter.format(rAu) + " AU";
      orbitDistanceKm.textContent = orbitFormatter.format(rKm / 1e6) + " million km";
      orbitSpeed.textContent = orbitFormatter.format(state.speedKmS) + " km/s";
      orbitSpeedNote.textContent = degrees <= 10 || degrees >= 350 ? "Near perihelion" : degrees >= 170 && degrees <= 190 ? "Near aphelion" : degrees < 180 ? "Moving toward aphelion" : "Moving toward perihelion";
      orbitPeri.textContent = orbitFormatter.format(periAu) + " AU";
      orbitAphe.textContent = orbitFormatter.format(apheAu) + " AU";
    }

    function animateOrbit(timestamp: number) {
      if (orbitAnimationStart === null) orbitAnimationStart = timestamp;
      const elapsed = (timestamp - orbitAnimationStart) % ORBIT_CYCLE_MS;
      const option = orbitSelect?.selectedOptions[0];
      const eccentricity = Number(option?.dataset.e);
      if (!orbitAngle || !Number.isFinite(eccentricity) || eccentricity < 0 || eccentricity >= 1) {
        stopOrbitAnimation();
        return;
      }
      const meanAnomaly = startingMeanAnomaly + (2 * Math.PI * elapsed / ORBIT_CYCLE_MS);
      const trueAnomaly = trueAnomalyFromMeanAnomaly(meanAnomaly, eccentricity);
      orbitAngle.value = String(Math.round(trueAnomaly * 10) / 10);
      updateOrbit();
      orbitAnimationFrame = requestAnimationFrame(animateOrbit);
    }

    orbitPlay?.addEventListener("click", () => {
      if (orbitAnimationFrame) {
        stopOrbitAnimation();
        return;
      }
      if (window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches) {
        if (orbitPlayStatus) orbitPlayStatus.textContent = "Animation is disabled by your reduced-motion setting. You can still use the slider.";
        return;
      }
      const option = orbitSelect?.selectedOptions[0];
      const eccentricity = Number(option?.dataset.e);
      const currentAngle = Number(orbitAngle?.value);
      if (!orbitAngle || !Number.isFinite(eccentricity) || eccentricity < 0 || eccentricity >= 1 || !Number.isFinite(currentAngle)) return;
      startingMeanAnomaly = meanAnomalyFromTrueAnomaly(currentAngle, eccentricity);
      orbitAnimationStart = null;
      orbitPlay.textContent = "Pause orbit";
      orbitPlay.setAttribute("aria-pressed", "true");
      if (orbitPlayStatus) orbitPlayStatus.textContent = "Playing one orbit in 24 seconds. The planet moves faster near perihelion and slower near aphelion.";
      orbitAnimationFrame = requestAnimationFrame(animateOrbit);
    });

    orbitSelect?.addEventListener("change", () => {
      stopOrbitAnimation(true);
      updateOrbit();
    });
    orbitAngle?.addEventListener("input", () => {
      stopOrbitAnimation(true);
      updateOrbit();
    });
    updateOrbit();

    if (window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches && orbitPlay) {
      orbitPlay.disabled = true;
      orbitPlay.setAttribute("aria-label", "Orbit animation disabled because reduced motion is enabled");
      if (orbitPlayStatus) orbitPlayStatus.textContent = "Animation is disabled by your reduced-motion setting. Use the slider to move the planet.";
    }
  </script>
  <style>
    .tools-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:16px}.tool-panel{scroll-margin-top:100px}.tool-panel h2{font-size:1.8rem;margin:10px 0}.tool-panel>p{font-size:.84rem;line-height:1.75;min-height:70px}.tool-footnote{font-size:.71rem!important;color:var(--quiet);line-height:1.65!important;min-height:0!important;margin:14px 0 0}.tool-panel .result-box strong{font-size:1.55rem}.size-stage{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:20px;min-height:155px;padding:20px;margin-top:18px;background:radial-gradient(ellipse at 24% 50%,rgba(67,100,146,.2),transparent 55%),#0a1220;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:6px}.size-orb{flex:0 0 auto;max-width:188px;max-height:188px;border-radius:50%;background:radial-gradient(circle at 30% 25%,#b4e2ed,#4585ad 45%,#173b63 82%);box-shadow:inset -15px -9px 18px #0006,0 0 25px #5294c455;transition:width .2s,height .2s}.size-stage strong,.size-stage span,.size-stage b{display:block}.size-stage strong{font:600 1.1rem "Space Grotesk",sans-serif}.size-stage span{font-size:.76rem;color:var(--muted);margin:3px 0 10px}.size-stage b{display:block;font-size:.75rem;color:var(--gold)}.size-stage small{display:block;color:var(--cyan);font-size:.72rem;margin-top:5px}.scale-legend{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;color:var(--quiet);font-size:.7rem;margin:12px 0 6px}.scale-track{height:7px;border-radius:99px;background:#24344b;overflow:hidden}.scale-track span{display:block;height:100%;border-radius:99px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#9bc6df,#e6c88e);transition:width .2s}.orbit-lab{margin-top:18px;padding:27px;scroll-margin-top:100px}.orbit-lab-heading{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-start;gap:25px;margin-bottom:20px}.orbit-lab-heading h2{font-size:1.9rem;margin:8px 0}.orbit-lab-heading p{max-width:690px;font-size:.86rem;line-height:1.75;margin:0}.orbit-lab-layout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr .9fr;gap:22px}.orbit-canvas{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:7px;background:radial-g